window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["story-v-y1v3-index"]=[{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p10-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner narration","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"ch 1  cold open in her pov  the icarus gamble the volume opens inside chabashira s first person with no setting and no interlocutor   a soliloquy that retells the myth of daedalus and icarus and then states why she provoked a certain young boy  the myth  her summary  daedalus  confined in a tower by king minos alongside his son icarus  fashions wings of bird feathers  thread and wax  the warning  if you fly too high  the sun will melt the wax holding the wings together  be careful  icarus forgets it  the wax melts  and he falls into the sea and dies   for some reason  i thought of icarus  wings when standing before a certain young boy   considering what these past few months had brought  i could say that i made the comparison simply because he resembled icarus   but i immediately came to realize that the two boys were fundamentally different from one another  this boy possessed neither the bravery nor the arrogance of icarus   i had been pushed into a corner  i had no choice but to do it   the die cannot be returned once cast  the gamble had already begun","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p10-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p10-1\">Ch.1: cold open in her POV, the Icarus gamble<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.10–12<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The volume opens inside Chabashira&#x27;s first person with no setting and no interlocutor — a soliloquy that retells the myth of Daedalus and Icarus and then states why she provoked a certain young boy.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> The myth, her summary: Daedalus, confined in a tower by King Minos alongside his son Icarus, fashions wings of bird feathers, thread and wax; the warning “If you fly too high, the sun will melt the wax holding the wings together.…<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;For some reason, I thought of Icarus’ wings when standing before a certain young boy.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> &quot;Considering what these past few months had brought, I could say that I made the comparison simply because he resembled Icarus.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Narration<\/span> The myth, her summary: Daedalus, confined in a tower by King Minos alongside his son Icarus, fashions wings of bird feathers, thread and wax; the warning “If you fly too high, the sun will melt the wax holding the wings together. Be careful.”; Icarus forgets it, the wax melts, and he falls into the sea and dies.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> She frames her own predicament in classical myth — “Greek mythology deals abundantly with human frailty.” — treating her situation as a fable to be interpreted before it is confessed.<span class=\"pg\">p.10<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;But I immediately came to realize that the two boys were fundamentally different from one another. This boy possessed neither the bravery nor the arrogance of Icarus.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;I had been pushed into a corner. I had no choice but to do it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Goal<\/span> Cornered and out of means, she chose the provocation: incur the boy&#x27;s divine wrath and turn his quiet rage onto herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> &quot;The die cannot be returned once cast. The gamble had already begun.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Soliloquy register: measured, literary, fatalistic — she narrates her own decision as a fable already decided, with no hedging and no appeal for sympathy.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–11<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The boy is never named on these pages — only &quot;a certain young boy&quot; / &quot;this boy&quot;. Identity left open; not assigned from context.<span class=\"pg\">p.10–11<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: she runs the rules that sink the summer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p13-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner narration","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 0  the cruise  the first name fever  and the boundary deck of the luxury liner on the way to the school s private island  first years of class d around him after midterms and finals  the chapter is his first person account   the endless summer sea  the infinite blue skies  the perfectly clear air  prices the trip honestly  on his own it  would probably have cost me about 100 000 yen  even in the off season  notes hirata s arrival as rescue   i was saved by the appearance of my hero  hirata man  on hirata and karuizawa cooling off   they seemed to get along well whenever i saw them talking  the chapter s thesis  stated before he understands it   i had yet to realize that this place was going to be the boundary between heaven and hell","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: the cruise, the first-name fever, and the boundary<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.13–23<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the luxury liner on the way to the school&#x27;s private island; first-years of Class D around him after midterms and finals.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q narration\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> The chapter is his first-person account: &quot;The endless summer sea. The infinite blue skies. The perfectly clear air.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Prices the trip honestly: on his own it &quot;would probably have cost me about 100,000 yen, even in the off season.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Notes Hirata&#x27;s arrival as rescue: &quot;I was saved by the appearance of my hero, Hirata Man.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Shoved by a Class A boy (&quot;Hey, you&#x27;re in the way. Move it, you defects.&quot;) and catches the railing; Sudou answers back, Class D is chased from the bow.<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Reads the hierarchy and swallows it: &quot;Although the situation was unfair, we didn&#x27;t need any unnecessary trouble, so it was best to ignore it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> On Hirata and Karuizawa cooling off: &quot;They seemed to get along well whenever I saw them talking.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Voice<\/span> Feeds Sudou&#x27;s practice by inventing a wrong first name — &quot;Tomiko. Horikita Tomiko.&quot; — then corrects it to Suzune; keeps the joke to himself.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Suspects Horikita&#x27;s hiding (&quot;a slight difference—something felt out of place&quot;) but drops it: &quot;it would be silly to investigate further. Best just to drop it.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.22–23<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s thesis, stated before he understands it: &quot;I had yet to realize that this place was going to be the boundary between heaven and hell.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1–2.2: the test is announced, and Class D splits three ways<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p13-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"sudou-ken kushida-kikyou mashima-tomonari ike-kanji","q":"ch 2  2 0    2 4  the cruise loudmouth who turns out to be the useful one deck of the liner  he opens the chapter with both hands in the air   whoa  this is the beeeeeeesssssst","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0 &amp; §2.4: the cruise loudmouth who turns out to be the useful one<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.13–17, p.67–70<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; he opens the chapter with both hands in the air.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#mashima-tomonari\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “Whoa! This is the beeeeeeesssssst!”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Teased by Yamauchi about his low final score; Sudou howls it off — &quot;With my skills, there was nothing to worry about.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.13–14<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Declares the trip the occasion to confess; secures first-name permission — “Of course it’s okay for you to call me that. Should I call you Kanjikun, then?” — and cries the answer out to heaven.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Substitutes for Ayanokōji as Sudou&#x27;s practice-Horikita and gets choke-held for the gyaru performance.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> The complaint Mashima answers seriously — &quot;We can’t all sleep together in just two tents!&quot; — which Mashima treats as a student operating below the programme&#x27;s level.<span class=\"pg\">p.26–27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Drinks the river on demand when challenged — &quot;Ah! Whew, that’s ice cold. It feels great! It’s damn good!&quot; — and gets the girls&#x27; disgust instead of trust.<span class=\"pg\">p.67–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The camping background surfaces properly: family trips as a child; he can read a clean water source on sight; first-ever expressed regret — &quot;I guess the stuff I said was probably a little unreasonable.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69–70<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p85-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.7–2.8: the bonfire, the apology, and the river vote<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v3-p13-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke shinohara-satsuki yamauchi-haruki karuizawa-kei","q":"ch 2  she is the girls  standard  and she bends for the class points deck of the liner  the group of girls  led by karuizawa  comes out of the cabin  and she points at the ocean with a radiant smile   this view is incredible  i m honestly super moved right now","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v3-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html#sc-karuizawa-kei-y1v3-p13-1\">Ch.2: she is the girls&#x27; standard, and she bends for the class points<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.13, p.42, p.96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; the group of girls &quot;led by Karuizawa&quot; comes out of the cabin, and she points at the ocean with a radiant smile.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#shinohara-satsuki\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> “This view is incredible! I’m honestly super moved right now!”<span class=\"pg\">p.13<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The chapter opens on the pair cooling off — &quot;lately she and Hirata haven’t been very flirty with each other&quot; — without a fight and without tension.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> The unexpected toilet answer: “Well, I suppose it’ll be tough, but I really want class points. I guess I’ll just grin and bear it.” — and the block moves: &quot;If Karuizawa said as much, then even the strong-willed Shinohara couldn’t oppose her openly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The endurance stance nobody predicted from her; Ayanokōji flags it as &quot;An unexpected response from Karuizawa, who seemed like she would’ve been first to complain.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Head of the &quot;Empress Team&quot; in Yamauchi&#x27;s map of the girls&#x27; groups.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p13-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ike-kanji sudou-ken","q":"ch 2  2 0  the cruise  the class a shove  and the name practice deck of the liner  survives the joke about his expulsion scoring final   with my skills  there was nothing to worry about  didn t i tell you i d prove myself  and it d be easy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: the cruise, the Class A shove, and the name practice<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.13–19<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; survives the joke about his expulsion-scoring final.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> “With my skills, there was nothing to worry about. Didn’t I tell you I’d prove myself, and it’d be easy?”<span class=\"pg\">p.14<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Answers a Class A shove with intimidation and is talked down by the situation, not by fear — &quot;A fistfight didn’t break out, evidence that he was perhaps growing up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.15–16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Forces Ayanokōji into imaginary-Horikita practice so he can ask for her first name; the look &quot;really creeped me out.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.17–19<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Puts Ike in a chokehold for the gyaru performance.<span class=\"pg\">p.19<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1–§2.5: the toilet, the leader card, and a first calm intervention<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p13-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka ibuki-mio yamauchi-haruki","q":"ch 2  2 0 2 8  the target switch  the matches  and bringing ibuki in deck of the liner  insults sudou about his near expulsion while sudou laughs it off","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p13-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html#sc-yamauchi-haruki-y1v3-p13-1\">Ch.2 §2.0–§2.8: the target-switch, the matches, and bringing Ibuki in<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.13–17, p.73–98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; insults Sudou about his near-expulsion while Sudou laughs it off.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Goes oddly quiet during Ike&#x27;s Kushida campaign; never raises the subject again.<span class=\"pg\">p.16–17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Confides the plan in a whisper — &quot;I think…I’m gonna go for Sakura&quot; — framing her as the reachable backup after Kushida; asks Ayanokōji to leave him alone with her.<span class=\"pg\">p.73–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gets refused and recovers instantly — &quot;Jeez, you’re stiff. Well, fine.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Burns three matches and gets only smoke; runs off to ask the teacher and comes back to Ike&#x27;s finished fire.<span class=\"pg\">p.83–84<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The one who won&#x27;t walk past the swollen-cheeked Class C girl; insists the three of them wait until she moves.<span class=\"pg\">p.80–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Explains her situation to the class when Satō notices the interloper.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Maps the girls&#x27; teams for the boys — &quot;the Empress Team, led by Karuizawa… Kushida-chan’s Friendship Team… Shinohara’s Arrogant Team. Then you have Horikita and Sakura, who are by themselves&quot; — and wants to eat with the last of them.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p14-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji horikita-suzune ibuki-mio sakura-airi kushida-kikyou","q":"ch 2  the first name permission  the leader nomination  and the shared meal deck of the liner  the extraordinary view  had stolen her breath away","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p14-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html#sc-kushida-kikyou-y1v3-p14-1\">Ch.2: the first-name permission, the leader nomination, and the shared meal<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.14–20, p.66–96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; the extraordinary view &quot;had stolen her breath away.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Grants Ike first-name permission and offers &quot;Kanjikun&quot; in return — the exchange that sets Ike&#x27;s confession plan running.<span class=\"pg\">p.17<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Present when Sudou fumbles Horikita&#x27;s first name as Tomiko; the correction to Suzune lands in front of the group.<span class=\"pg\">p.18<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Nominates Horikita as spot-leader in the circle — Hirata and Karuizawa &quot;stand out too much,&quot; but responsibility is the criterion: &quot;I think that Horikita-san meets that criteria.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Ayanokōji reads the nomination as the least-risk play: Horikita &quot;was so desperate to reach Class A. That was crucial.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Walks over with a meal seat and water from her own group&#x27;s ration — four people sharing three portions — while Ibuki protests &quot;Are you guys stupid? You’re all being way too nice.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95–96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s last word on her: &quot;Kushida, who wished for everyone’s happiness, had charity to spare.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Raises her hand for river water once the vote is already tipping, which Ayanokōji suspects is influence rather than conviction.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei horikita-suzune ike-kanji hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 0 2 2  the leader tries to hold a class that won t hold still deck of the liner  he pulls ayanokoji into the group the moment he appears","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1\">Ch.2 §2.0–2.2: the leader tries to hold a class that won&#x27;t hold still<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.16, p.30–51<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner; he pulls Ayanokōji into the group the moment he appears.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Called over as rescue; Hirata himself is too busy — &quot;Miyake-kun looks like he&#x27;s having trouble&quot; — and leaves for the cabins.<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Asked why he isn&#x27;t with her: “We just kind of take things at our own pace.”<span class=\"pg\">p.16<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Reads the watch rule as safety kit, not control: &quot;the school had gifted us these watches to keep us safe.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Opened the rules huddle that Ike&#x27;s complaints fracture into factions.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Breaks his own neutrality on the toilet: &quot;I&#x27;ve thought it over, and I believe we should install one toilet first&quot; — then beats Yukimura&#x27;s objection with the arithmetic of thirty-plus students sharing one box.<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s verdict on the method: &quot;It wasn’t just to provoke arguments; he was convinced that he’d get their approval eventually.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.51<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4–2.8: the river, the 120-point speech, and taking Ibuki in<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 0  she comes down from the ship wrong deck of the liner at disembark call  class d waits in the heat   i was just reading a book in my room  for whom the bell tolls  you wouldn t know it","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1\">Ch.2 §2.0: she comes down from the ship wrong<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.22–23<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deck of the liner at disembark call; Class D waits in the heat.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I was just reading a book in my room. For Whom the Bell Tolls. You wouldn’t know it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> &quot;Even Horikita, normally so meticulous, was concerned about her appearance. Right now, though, her hair was disheveled.&quot; — and she rubs her arms as if cold.<span class=\"pg\">p.22<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Her stated excuse for locking herself away doesn&#x27;t cover what Ayanokōji saw; the chapter leaves the gap open.<span class=\"pg\">p.23<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.1: she asks the questions that price the test<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner","w":"horikita-suzune hoshinomiya-chie ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 1 2 2  the test is announced  and class d splits three ways beach landing  mashima sensei announces the deserted island special test from a white platform  names the test s real shape   essentially  it was a contest of restraint","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1\">Ch.2 §2.1–2.2: the test is announced, and Class D splits three ways<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.24–46<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Beach landing; Mashima-sensei announces the deserted-island special test from a white platform.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Names the test&#x27;s real shape: &quot;Essentially, it was a contest of restraint.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.32<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Works the rules the way the chapter needs them read: the penalties page &quot;will determine whether you live or die&quot;; the watches are safety kit — &quot;the school had gifted us these watches to keep us safe.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30–31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> First to ask the question that sets the economy: &quot;is it possible to get by without using any points?&quot; — Chabashira answers that the school &quot;isn&#x27;t involved in the test process at all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands apart from the toilet fight, watching Hirata get pulled apart: &quot;I stood a short distance away, watching the situation unfold.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Sidles up to her read of the class; she admits she can&#x27;t see a solution and he agrees — &quot;I think the same. There&#x27;s too much we don&#x27;t know.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Given the season-opening advice about confessing to a girl before the ocean; wishes she would leave his love life alone.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: the cruise, the first-name fever, and the boundary<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2–2.3: he volunteers, and Horikita&#x27;s isolation is priced<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hoshinomiya-chie ike-kanji chabashira-sae","q":"ch 2  2 1  she runs the rules that sink the summer beach landing  she takes class d s roll call in the same jersey as the students   keeping on like that would be shameful  ike  so stop talking    and the world widening follow up   there are workplaces where there aren t any chairs in the office  and companies that decide salaries with dice rolls  the world is wider and deeper than you even know   in other words  you are ill equipped to distinguish between what is reality and what isn t     in my opinion  you re all equally worthless","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: she runs the rules that sink the summer<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.24–39<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Beach landing; she takes Class D&#x27;s roll call in the same jersey as the students.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “Keeping on like that would be shameful, Ike, so stop talking.” — and the world-widening follow-up: “There are workplaces where there aren’t any chairs in the office, and companies that decide salaries with dice rolls. The world…”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> “In other words, you are ill-equipped to distinguish between what is reality and what isn’t.” / “In my opinion, you’re all equally worthless.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26–27<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Keeping on like that would be shameful, Ike, so stop talking.” — and the world-widening follow-up: “There are workplaces where there aren’t any chairs in the office, and companies that decide salaries with dice rolls. The world is wider and deeper than you even know.”<span class=\"pg\">p.26<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Delivers the penalty list verbatim from the manual — thirty for health retirement, twenty for pollution, five per absent student at roll call, disqualification plus private-point forfeiture for inter-class violence.<span class=\"pg\">p.31<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Assembles the cardboard toilet in front of the class and demonstrates the polymer sheet — &quot;five uses with one vinyl bag.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Explains the spot system: eight-hour rights of exclusive possession, one provisional bonus point per occupation, fifty-point penalty for using another class&#x27;s spot.<span class=\"pg\">p.39<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> Brushes off the eavesdropping complaint and the &quot;fate&quot; line; threatens a behavioural report.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Refuses the emergency-bear question on process grounds: &quot;the test has already begun. I cannot answer any questions that might possibly influence your results.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.30<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Confirms the school &quot;isn’t involved in the test process at all&quot; — survival is the test.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p10-1\">← Before: Ch.1: cold open in her POV, the Icarus gamble<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.8: she announces the retirement<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v3-p24-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji mashima-tomonari","q":"ch 2  2 1  the announcement that erases the vacation a prepared white platform on the beach  uniformed adults setting up a tent and computers behind him   well then  we shall commence the current academic year s first special test   this test will determine if you can live on a deserted island together as a group  designed based on real world corporate training  sets the theme that names the chapter   the theme of this special exam is  freedom  after all","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-mashima-tomonari-y1v3-p24-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1: the announcement that erases the vacation<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.24–29<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#mashima-tomonari\">Mashima Tomonari<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A prepared white platform on the beach; uniformed adults setting up a tent and computers behind him.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “Well then. We shall commence the current academic year’s first special test.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> “This test will determine if you can live on a deserted island together as a group… designed based on real-world corporate training.”<span class=\"pg\">p.25<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Mashima Tomonari<\/b> Sets the theme that names the chapter: &quot;The theme of this special exam is ‘freedom’, after all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Post<\/span> Introduced as Class A&#x27;s homeroom teacher, English, &quot;well-known for having a stubborn disposition,&quot; built like a wrestler but &quot;actually quite intelligent&quot; — and he opens grim: &quot;it’s unfortunate that one of you was unable to participate due to illness.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.24<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Answers Ike&#x27;s disbelief without contempt for the complaint itself, only for its basis — &quot;you’ve lived a short, superficial life. There is an actual, prominent company that holds training sessions on uninhabited islands.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.26–27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Concedes the process complaint where he didn&#x27;t concede the disbelief: &quot;I suppose that you’re not wrong about that. I can understand why you would be discontented.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.27<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Hands out the three-hundred-point budget and the manual; frames the week as playable.<span class=\"pg\">p.27–28<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Names the stakes — remaining points convert to class points after vacation — and the Class A illness penalty: thirty points, leaving A at 270.<span class=\"pg\">p.28–29<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v3-p32-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ike-kanji karuizawa-kei hirata-yousuke yukimura-teruhiko shinohara-satsuki","q":"ch 2  2 1  the toilet war rules huddle on the beach  the cardboard toilet demonstration lands on the girls   don t tell me we have to use that    raised  in horrified surprise  at the assembled box","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v3-p32-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.1: the toilet war<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.32–35, p.41–42<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#shinohara-satsuki\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Rules huddle on the beach; the cardboard toilet demonstration lands on the girls.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yukimura-teruhiko\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> “Don’t tell me we have to use that?!” — raised &quot;in horrified surprise&quot; at the assembled box.<span class=\"pg\">p.34<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The argument that runs the section: &quot;Don’t screw around! It probably doesn’t matter to you boys.&quot; / &quot;It’s true though, isn’t it? You do seem to be really perverted.&quot; / &quot;A gentleman? Get real. You’re by far the top contender for biggest pervert.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.35<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Begs the girls&#x27; representative to back the 20-point temporary toilet — &quot;Karuizawa-san, say something, will you?&quot; — and is outvoted by Karuizawa&#x27;s endurance line.<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Keeps pleading with Hirata as the only decision-maker she trusts: &quot;Hirata-kun is going to consider all of our opinions and decide. Right, Hirata-kun?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> Gets the discrimination charge from him for framing it as a girls-only need: &quot;Isn’t that simply a form of discrimination?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v3-p67-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4–§2.8: the river fight, the apology, and the vote<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 1  she asks the questions that price the test class d s first rules huddle on the beach after mashima s announcement   in the event that someone were to retire after we had already used all 300 points  what would happen    the question that establishes the floor at zero   i m the same as the others  i ve never lived in such an environment before  so i can t really make any predictions  what an unpleasant test    her first open admission that academics don t transfer here","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: she asks the questions that price the test<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.33–45<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class D&#x27;s first rules huddle on the beach after Mashima&#x27;s announcement.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “In the event that someone were to retire after we had already used all 300 points, what would happen?” — the question that establishes the floor at zero.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I’m the same as the others. I’ve never lived in such an environment before, so I can’t really make any predictions… What an unpleasant test.” — her first open admission that academics don&#x27;t transfer here.<span class=\"pg\">p.44<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Stands beside Ayanokōji watching Hirata fail to decide: &quot;Class D has no leadership, which worries me. Besides, Hirata’s a pushover. He can’t even make one decision, can he?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.43–44<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks him to take her side on endurance; he agrees; Classes A and B are already moving into the forest while C and D still can&#x27;t start.<span class=\"pg\">p.44–45<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p22-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: she comes down from the ship wrong<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.2: she admits the isolation, and blocks the probe<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p33-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"horikita-suzune shinohara-satsuki ayanokouji-kiyotaka sudou-ken","q":"ch 2  2 1 2 5  the toilet  the leader card  and a first calm intervention","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p33-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html#sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p33-1\">Ch.2 §2.1–§2.5: the toilet, the leader card, and a first calm intervention<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.33, p.66–74<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#shinohara-satsuki\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Opens the cardboard-toilet crisis by needing it before the explanation is finished.<span class=\"pg\">p.33<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Steps forward to take the leader role in her place — &quot;You don’t want to do it though, right? Don’t make her do it. I can do it in her place.&quot; — and the offer is what triggers her acceptance.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Chides her in an unusually calm tone — &quot;I know I’ve caused trouble for the class. That’s what I’m saying.&quot; — and offers the boiling compromise nobody expected from him.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Self-aware about his own record: &quot;If you keep antagonizing people with trivial crap, eventually it’s gonna come back to bite you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Refuses the branch run flatly and goes swimming instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-sudou-ken-y1v3-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0: the cruise, the Class A shove, and the name practice<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v3-p36-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"chabashira-sae ayanokouji-kiyotaka hoshinomiya-chie","q":"ch 2  2 1  the corridor ambush beach side  during class d s rules huddle  she tackles chabashira from behind   what  i can t be friendly  i honestly wanted to see what you d do     whenever i touch your hair  sae chan  it s always so smooth   you need to be more carefree","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v3-p36-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html#sc-hoshinomiya-chie-y1v3-p36-1\">Ch.2 §2.1: the corridor ambush<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.36–38<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hoshinomiya-chie.html\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Beach-side, during Class D&#x27;s rules huddle; she tackles Chabashira from behind.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “What, I can’t be friendly? I honestly wanted to see what you’d do.” / “Whenever I touch your hair, Sae-chan, it’s always so smooth!”<span class=\"pg\">p.36<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hoshinomiya Chie<\/b> “You need to be more carefree!”<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Chabashira Sae<\/b> Gets the eavesdropping rebuke and the &quot;fate&quot; double-meaning ignored; leaves with a sad look when threatened with a behavioural report.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Spots him and opens the summer-love advice — &quot;Summer is the season of love. If you want to confess your feelings to a girl you like, perhaps it’d be more effective while standing before the beautiful ocean?&quot; — to his visible embarrassment.<span class=\"pg\">p.38<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v3-p42-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ike-kanji kouenji-rokusuke yukimura-teruhiko","q":"ch 2  the no points hardliner  and the day he folds joins the toilet fight uninvited  sliding his glasses up   it s not as though i don t understand the girls  desire to have a temporary toilet  however  i m not convinced that we ought to arbitrarily spend our points  i d like to at least make a decision after collecting a majority vote","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-yukimura-teruhiko-y1v3-p42-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2: the no-points hardliner, and the day he folds<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.42–43, p.50–51, p.90, p.98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yukimura-teruhiko\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Joins the toilet fight uninvited, sliding his glasses up.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> “It’s not as though I don’t understand the girls’ desire to have a temporary toilet. However, I’m not convinced that we ought to arbitrarily spend our points… I’d like to at least make a decision after collecting a majority vote.”<span class=\"pg\">p.42<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The line the chapter keeps against him: “Even money can move based purely on instinct. I hate that women argue so emotionally.” — and Shinohara&#x27;s &quot;Huh?&quot; is the only response printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.43<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Loses the toilet vote to Hirata&#x27;s arithmetic — &quot;Fine. In that case, let’s install one toilet.&quot; — described as beaten: &quot;Yukimura, who couldn’t bear being stared at in silence, broke.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.50–51<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Folds again when Ike sides with Hirata&#x27;s 120-point plan: &quot;Yukimura still appeared reluctant, but seeing Ike join with Hirata made him fold.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> The outburst at the retirement — &quot;Kouenji, you jerk! What the hell…were you thinking?!&quot; — &quot;The normally silent Yukimura shouted and kicked the ground.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner","w":"horikita-suzune sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 2 2 3  he volunteers  and horikita s isolation is priced walking from beach toward the forest with the tent party  horikita trails the group alone  his standing theory of her  filed as interpretation not fact   horikita had enrolled here to be at the same school as her older brother  she wasn t aiming for class a for her own sake  but rather  sought her older brother s approval","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1\">Ch.2 §2.2–2.3: he volunteers, and Horikita&#x27;s isolation is priced<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.47–52<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking from beach toward the forest with the tent party; Horikita trails the group alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> His standing theory of her, filed as interpretation not fact: &quot;Horikita had enrolled here to be at the same school as her older brother. She wasn&#x27;t aiming for Class A for her own sake, but rather, sought her older brother&#x27;s…<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Her depression out loud — &quot;I can&#x27;t be alone&quot; — and his answer that this test is the one her academics can&#x27;t win; he watches her realise Ike and Sudou moved faster than she could.<span class=\"pg\">p.47–48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> His standing theory of her, filed as interpretation not fact: &quot;Horikita had enrolled here to be at the same school as her older brother. She wasn&#x27;t aiming for Class A for her own sake, but rather, sought her older brother&#x27;s approval.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She blocks the probe — &quot;It doesn&#x27;t feel good to have someone pry into your past&quot; — and he retreats cleanly.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Raises his hand for the search party for a stated system reason: &quot;without a role to fill in the class, you&#x27;ll get cut off.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Paired by leftovers&#x27; logic with Sakura and Kouenji; notes the pairing works — &quot;I&#x27;d be able to move without any difficulty.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.52<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p24-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1–2.2: the test is announced, and Class D splits three ways<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.3: the forest team, and Class A&#x27;s leader in the open<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 2  she admits the isolation  and blocks the probe walking from beach to forest  she trails the group alone   to be honest  i m depressed  these kinds of things just aren t for me  life on an island seems primitive  and worst of all  i can t be alone   it doesn t feel good to have someone pry into your past    and names chabashira as the leak   chabashira sensei leaked the information  don t misunderstand me  all right  besides  we re still not friends  don t forget that","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\">Ch.2 §2.2: she admits the isolation, and blocks the probe<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.47–49<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking from beach to forest; she trails the group alone.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “To be honest, I’m depressed. These kinds of things just aren’t for me. Life on an island seems primitive, and worst of all, I can’t be alone.”<span class=\"pg\">p.47<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “It doesn’t feel good to have someone pry into your past” — and names Chabashira as the leak: “Chabashira-sensei leaked the information. Don’t misunderstand me. All right? Besides, we’re still not friends. Don’t forget that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Concedes the classroom verdict against her own tools: &quot;This test will likely fall outside of my academic abilities. I’d determined that Ike-kun and Sudou-kun would be hindrances, but they took the initiative to go out searching. I wasn’t able to do anything.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.48<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Ends the exchange on her own terms before he can go deeper.<span class=\"pg\">p.49<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p33-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: she asks the questions that price the test<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4: the leader&#x27;s card, and the favour she can&#x27;t do herself<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p48-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kouenji-rokusuke horikita-suzune yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi","q":"ch 2  the forest team  the blush  and the second volunteer shift walking from beach to forest  she is at the back  watching ayanokoji s back   and looks away when he turns","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p48-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html#sc-sakura-airi-y1v3-p48-1\">Ch.2: the forest team, the blush, and the second volunteer shift<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.48, p.52–63, p.74–97<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking from beach to forest; she is at the back, watching Ayanokōji&#x27;s back — and looks away when he turns.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>10 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Leftover-paired with him and Kouenji; trips on roots and he pulls her up, brushing dirt from her hands — &quot;S-sorry.&quot; / &quot;You don’t need to apologize.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.53–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Flusters and hurries forward when he asks why she raised her hand: &quot;Th-that’s not what I mean! It’s just that since there isn’t anyone I can talk to, that’s why…&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.54<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Lends her handkerchief for the trail marker without hesitation.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Goes &quot;almost comatose&quot; when he holds her hand through the Class A hide — &quot;I thought I was going to die. My heart stopped…&quot; — and adjusts her glasses as she recovers.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–61<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/b> Surprisingly harsh on him in the moment: &quot;Kouenji-kun has been acting pretty funny from the start, so it’s okay.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Scared off by a single sharp look — &quot;Were you looking at me just now?&quot; — and runs to put distance between them.<span class=\"pg\">p.63–64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Second volunteer shift, the branch run, after Sudou and Yamauchi refuse; &quot;if I stay here, well…it’ll be…a little uncomfortable.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.74–75<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Asks whether he should have taken Ike&#x27;s fire credit himself; his answer moves her — &quot;like she was moved by my words.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Eats alone at the edge of the groups; the boys&#x27; attention lands on her body while the chapter keeps her out of the conversation entirely.<span class=\"pg\">p.96–97<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Yamauchi&#x27;s map of the class: she and Horikita are the two girls &quot;who are by themselves.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v3-p52-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yukimura-teruhiko kouenji-rokusuke","q":"ch 2  2 3    2 8  the forest walk  and the retirement that costs thirty points volunteer circle for the forest search  he raises a hand last   the sun certainly is refreshing  my body needs energy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v3-p52-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html#sc-kouenji-rokusuke-y1v3-p52-1\">Ch.2 §2.3 &amp; §2.8: the forest walk, and the retirement that costs thirty points<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.52–63, p.97–98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kouenji-rokusuke.html\">Kōenji Rokusuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Volunteer circle for the forest search; he raises a hand last, &quot;The sun certainly is refreshing. My body needs energy.&quot;<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#yukimura-teruhiko\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Answers Ayanokōji&#x27;s worry about getting lost with the perfect-human disclaimer — &quot;I am a perfect human being. I would never foolishly lose my way in a forest. If any problem occurs, it would most likely be because you two lost sight of me. When that happens, you should give up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.55–57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the island in one line: &quot;I wouldn’t call this a natural forest. The probability of getting lost during the day is extremely low. It’s precisely for that reason that I’m a little curious.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.56<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Poses the question the ordinary pair can&#x27;t answer — &quot;What do you see when you look around?&quot; — accepts &quot;Common folk are simple, after all,&quot; and walks on.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Skipped the return and went swimming; Ayanokōji notes he ran off &quot;suggesting that he was already familiar with the forest.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.63<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Retires from the test on a claimed poor physical condition; the class eats a thirty-point penalty; Chabashira states the rule — &quot;Kouenji has retired, and he’s obligated to stay onboard the ship for one week for medical treatment.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yukimura Teruhiko<\/b> The normally silent Yukimura shouts and kicks the ground at the news; the class is furious and can do nothing.<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 3  the forest team  and class a s leader in the open forest path with kouenji ahead and sakura behind  damp heat  unstable footing","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the forest team, and Class A&#x27;s leader in the open<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.53–62<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Forest path with Kouenji ahead and Sakura behind; damp heat, unstable footing.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Hides them both when a Class A boy leaves the cave; overhears Katsuragi name himself leader and the cave as a spot.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Talks to her because she is the only one left to talk to; she trips on roots and he pulls her up, brushing dirt from her hands.<span class=\"pg\">p.54–55<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Borrows Sakura&#x27;s handkerchief and ties it to a branch as a trail marker — the chapter&#x27;s first quiet competence beat.<span class=\"pg\">p.57<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Slows his own pace so Sakura won&#x27;t feel like the problem: &quot;That way, Sakura wouldn&#x27;t feel like the problem. She probably saw through my ploy, but I didn&#x27;t mind.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.58<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Works out the fatal leak on the spot — &quot;They had clearly made their leader known to us&quot; — and takes the report on himself so Sakura, who has poor communication skills, doesn&#x27;t have to carry it.<span class=\"pg\">p.61–62<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Holds her hand through the hiding without meaning to; she goes &quot;almost comatose&quot; and he checks on her twice.<span class=\"pg\">p.60–61<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p47-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2–2.3: he volunteers, and Horikita&#x27;s isolation is priced<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.4–2.5: the river camp, the leader vote, and Horikita&#x27;s favour<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p59-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"totsuka-yahiko sakayanagi-arisu ibuki-mio katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 2  2 3  the class a leader who showed his card a reinforced cave on the mountainside  he comes out and stands watch at the entrance","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p59-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.3: the Class A leader who showed his card<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.59–62<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#katsuragi-kouhei\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A reinforced cave on the mountainside; he comes out and stands watch at the entrance.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#sakayanagi-arisu\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Lectures his partner on the school&#x27;s hints — the ship&#x27;s deliberate circle around the island, the path visible from the deck — &quot;Finding it was inevitable. Be mindful of what you say and do.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s model of Class A thinking: &quot;Before the ship docked at the pier, it had already taken a trip around…the island as a detour for some reason. That was probably a deliberate move by the school to give the students some hints.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.59–60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> Named as the rival his partner expects to silence by holding the cave.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The contempt line that frames Class D: &quot;Class D is just an assortment of failures, right? They’re defective. Considering the point difference, it’s probably fine to ignore them, right?&quot; — overruled as enough chit-chat.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Identified by the watchers as Class A&#x27;s spot-leader holding the key card — a mistake Ayanokōji files as &quot;a fatal mistake&quot; for the seventh-day guess rule.<span class=\"pg\">p.61–62<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p127-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the parley at the cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p59-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"sakayanagi-arisu katsuragi-kouhei totsuka-yahiko","q":"ch 2  2 3  the second man in the cave inside and around the class a cave with katsuragi on day one   in a cave this size  we should have enough room for two tents  katsuragi san  we sure were lucky  we secured a spot really quickly    corrected on the spot  luck was inference   i didn t notice anything at all  and yet  katsuragi san  you managed to see the school s true intentions  because of that  you understood there was a cave here  just as we d expect from you","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p59-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html#sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p59-1\">Ch.2 §2.3: the second man in the cave<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.59–60<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Inside and around the Class A cave with Katsuragi on day one.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#sakayanagi-arisu\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#katsuragi-kouhei\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “In a cave this size, we should have enough room for two tents, Katsuragi-san. We sure were lucky. We secured a spot really quickly.” — corrected on the spot: luck was inference.<span class=\"pg\">p.59<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “I didn’t notice anything at all, and yet… Katsuragi-san, you managed to see the school’s true intentions. Because of that, you understood there was a cave here. Just as we’d expect from you!”<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakayanagi Arisu<\/b> “If we leave it like this, Sakayanagi will have no choice but to be quiet!” — the only Sakayanagi naming in the chapter.<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Carries the Class D contempt his leader overrules: &quot;Considering the point difference, it’s probably fine to ignore them, right?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.60<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: holding the entrance<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner","w":"horikita-suzune sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 4 2 5  the river camp  the leader vote  and horikita s favour back at the assembly point  ike s group reports a river with a possession device ten minutes away  prices her isolation as the test s real subject   an academically brilliant girl was less useful than a normal student in a situation like this  and  this week would test horikita suzune s limits  and show her at her worst","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1\">Ch.2 §2.4–2.5: the river camp, the leader vote, and Horikita&#x27;s favour<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.63–71<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Back at the assembly point; Ike&#x27;s group reports a river with a possession device ten minutes away.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Prices her isolation as the test&#x27;s real subject: &quot;An academically brilliant girl was less useful than a normal student in a situation like this.&quot; and &quot;This week would test Horikita Suzune&#x27;s limits, and show her at her worst.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Answer for both of them to her question about Kouenji — &quot;I can&#x27;t control that guy. You know that.&quot; — then deflects her glare when she asks what he said.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> In the leader vote, reads the room instead of speaking: Kushida&#x27;s nomination of Horikita is &quot;the least risky choice, since she was so desperate to reach Class A.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Personally relieved Sudou wasn&#x27;t chosen: &quot;I was relieved that someone like Sudou or Ike wasn&#x27;t the leader.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> She delegates the Ike problem to him — &quot;I&#x27;m relying on you because I know I can&#x27;t do it&quot; — and he takes the timing as his own: &quot;I&#x27;ll talk to him, but leave the timing to me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p53-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the forest team, and Class A&#x27;s leader in the open<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5–2.6: branches, Yamauchi&#x27;s plan, and the bonfire<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji horikita-suzune ibuki-mio sakura-airi kushida-kikyou hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 2  2 4 2 8  the river  the 120 point speech  and taking ibuki in receives ike s river report and moves the class toward a base camp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\">Ch.2 §2.4–2.8: the river, the 120-point speech, and taking Ibuki in<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.63–96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Receives Ike&#x27;s river report and moves the class toward a base camp.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Praised the find — &quot;Amazing, Ike-kun!&quot; — then takes his name to Chabashira as leader-candidate filing errand-boy.<span class=\"pg\">p.64<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Files Horikita&#x27;s name and hands her the card; orchestrates the fake collective touch to hide the leader.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Breaks up the Ike–Shinohara round two and buys time: &quot;Let’s try breaking apart for a bit. We still have some time.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Asks Ayanokōji for branches, apologetically — &quot;I can’t force you to agree&quot; — because light is necessary whether or not points get spent.<span class=\"pg\">p.72<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s centrepiece speech: sets the realistic floor at 120 points left, walks the class through the meal maths (10-point sets, 12 meals, 120 points), then reframes endurance as upside — &quot;If we can find drinking water for the week, we’ll save fifty points or more.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.89–90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Ayanokōji&#x27;s read: &quot;Anyone else could have come up with this, but Hirata’s tone and presentation sold it. He’d performed flawlessly.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Takes the injured Class C girl in: &quot;We can’t just leave someone in trouble. We all think so.&quot; — and turns the spy question on its head: &quot;If you really were a spy, you wouldn’t want to be chased out, would you?&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Leaves Sakura out of the Ibuki escort — Ayanokōji reads it as pretty-boy thoughtfulness.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Distributes the evening meal while Kushida feeds Ibuki from her own group&#x27;s portion.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p16-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0–2.2: the leader tries to hold a class that won&#x27;t hold still<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the morning watch and the point arithmetic<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"kushida-kikyou sudou-ken ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 4  the leader s card  and the favour she can t do herself the circle that picks class d s spot leader   i understand  i accept    after sudou tries to take the role to spare her","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\">Ch.2 §2.4: the leader&#x27;s card, and the favour she can&#x27;t do herself<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.63–71<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The circle that picks Class D&#x27;s spot-leader.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I understand. I accept.” — after Sudou tries to take the role to spare her.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Kushida nominates her as the responsible choice; she accepts without visible surprise.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Becomes Class D&#x27;s designated leader; Hirata files her name with Chabashira and the card is handed over; the class touches the device together to hide who holds it.<span class=\"pg\">p.66–67<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> His defence of her wishes is the trigger that makes her take the role rather than dodge it.<span class=\"pg\">p.66<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Delegates the Ike problem — &quot;I&#x27;m relying on you because I know I can&#x27;t do it. Can I count on you?&quot; — then delivers the standard put-down: “I suppose it must be relaxing to be unreliable and underachieving. … Isn’t it, Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.70–71<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> The chapter&#x27;s closing read of her: alone she is &quot;amazing…but only alone&quot;; the school &quot;had made her isolated life impossible.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.71<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p47-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.2: she admits the isolation, and blocks the probe<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.5 &amp; §2.8: she refuses the assistantship, and votes last<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v3-p67-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ike-kanji sudou-ken yamauchi-haruki shinohara-satsuki","q":"ch 2  2 4 2 8  the river fight  the apology  and the vote","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v3-p67-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.4–§2.8: the river fight, the apology, and the vote<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.67–68, p.88, p.91<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#shinohara-satsuki\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sudou-ken.html\">Sudō Ken<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The drinking-water round: &quot;Then you drink it, as an experiment.&quot; → his gulp → &quot;Okay, that’s a major turn off. No way, no way! … Gross!&quot; / &quot;No way! Ugh, I hate barbarians like you most of all, god!&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.67–68<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sudō Ken<\/b> Mocks Sudou&#x27;s cooperation line — &quot;Oh, don’t make me laugh. Cooperate? That’s funny coming from you, Sudou-kun.&quot; — and then tells him to stop with the thoughtful suggestions.<span class=\"pg\">p.68–69<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Accepts his apology and answers with her own: &quot;I think I got way too emotional. We won’t be able to keep any of our points if we don’t learn to adjust.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The holdout who converts last: &quot;I don’t know if I can drink it, but…I’m up for the challenge.&quot; — after Ike offers Sudou&#x27;s boiling plan as the on-ramp.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Head of the &quot;Arrogant Team&quot; in Yamauchi&#x27;s map of the girls&#x27; groups.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-shinohara-satsuki-y1v3-p32-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: the toilet war<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"yamauchi-haruki sakura-airi ike-kanji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 5 2 6  branches  yamauchi s plan  and the bonfire evening at the river camp  hirata asks him to gather branches for a bonfire","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1\">Ch.2 §2.5–2.6: branches, Yamauchi&#x27;s plan, and the bonfire<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.72–77<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Evening at the river camp; Hirata asks him to gather branches for a bonfire.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">After Sudou and Yamauchi refuse, Sakura volunteers and he lets her; Yamauchi then reverses and joins.<span class=\"pg\">p.74<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Yamauchi confides the switch from Kushida to Sakura as a body-driven target plan; he refuses the ask — &quot;I&#x27;d like to go back and start the bonfire while it&#x27;s still early.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76–77<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Declines on her behalf rather than leaving her alone with &quot;some guy who only wanted to get into her pants.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.76<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Diagnoses the failed fire when Yamauchi cannot — damp wood, branches too thick — and stays quiet so Ike can be the one to fix it.<span class=\"pg\">p.84–85<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Explains the quiet help to Sakura: &quot;building up Ike and displaying his usefulness will be more helpful to the class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4–2.5: the river camp, the leader vote, and Horikita&#x27;s favour<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.6–2.7: Ibuki, and the decision not to leave her<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune","q":"ch 2  2 5    2 8  she refuses the assistantship  and votes last","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\">Ch.2 §2.5 &amp; §2.8: she refuses the assistantship, and votes last<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.73–74, p.92<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> On becoming Hirata&#x27;s assistant: “Me, his assistant? Don’t joke around. I’d rather dance with a mongoose.”<span class=\"pg\">p.73<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Names her own usable condition — &quot;If there were a clear enemy and a goal, I might be of…use&quot; — and admits she still can&#x27;t decide how far the class should spend.<span class=\"pg\">p.73–74<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Raises her hand for river water last, with Ayanokōji, after the whole class has already committed.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4: the leader&#x27;s card, and the favour she can&#x27;t do herself<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: called out of the tent<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"ibuki-mio hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 6 2 7  ibuki  and the decision not to leave her walking back with branches  a girl from another class sits against a tree with a red  swollen mark on her cheek","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1\">Ch.2 §2.6–2.7: Ibuki, and the decision not to leave her<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.78–86<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking back with branches; a girl from another class sits against a tree with a red, swollen mark on her cheek.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Stops Yamauchi from walking past her; the three of them agree to wait rather than leave an injured girl in the jungle.<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Answers her &quot;I&#x27;m from Class C. In other words, I&#x27;m your enemy&quot; with &quot;That wasn&#x27;t any reason not to help.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Says the camp-location leak won&#x27;t be a problem when she names the risk — the chapter never says why he is sure.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Introduces himself properly and holds the space while Hirata works the crowd: &quot;Sorry. Can you wait a little longer? I&#x27;m going to talk to him about you.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Watches Hirata take Ibuki in and wonders why he was the one left with her: &quot;I wondered if Hirata had left me with her because he trusted me, or at least trusted me more than Yamauchi.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p72-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5–2.6: branches, Yamauchi&#x27;s plan, and the bonfire<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1\">→ After: Ch.2 §2.8: the points speech, the river vote, and Kouenji&#x27;s exit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka yamauchi-haruki hirata-yousuke kushida-kikyou ibuki-mio","q":"ch 2  2 6 2 8  the class c girl with the swollen cheek a path in the forest on the way back to camp  she sits against a large tree  not a class d student  with a red  swollen mark on her cheek","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1\">Ch.2 §2.6–§2.8: the Class C girl with the swollen cheek<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.78–96<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A path in the forest on the way back to camp; she sits against a large tree, not a Class D student, with a red, swollen mark on her cheek.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/yamauchi-haruki.html\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>9 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> &quot;Just a class dispute. Don’t worry about it&quot; — her answer when asked who did it; &quot;her voice was low and even, but it was clear she wasn’t feeling well.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.80<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Names the barrier herself: “I’m from Class C. In other words, I’m your enemy. You understand that, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.81<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Yamauchi Haruki<\/b> Refuses the base-camp offer — &quot;There’s no way I could do something like that&quot; — then watches them refuse to leave: &quot;You guys are really stupid. You’re not acting logically. You aren’t thinking about your own class.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.81–82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Introductions after the standoff: “I’m…Ibuki” — and she won&#x27;t meet his eyes.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Dirt under her nails and disturbed soil where she sat — the page shows the fight without naming who won it.<span class=\"pg\">p.82<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> The account, once Hirata&#x27;s offer sticks: &quot;I had a fight with a boy in my class. He hit me and chased me away. That’s all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.94–95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> On his decency: “He’s seriously a good-natured guy, isn’t he?” — and the Class C verdict: &quot;Not at all… There isn’t really anyone in Class C like that.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.95<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Gets Kushida&#x27;s group ration — &quot;Are you guys stupid? You’re all being way too nice.&quot; — and is told to eat first, talk later.<span class=\"pg\">p.96<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Told to wait while the class decides; the class agrees to shelter her once roll-call attrition makes it profitable, not only decent.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the camera in her bag<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p85-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"shinohara-satsuki hirata-yousuke sakura-airi ike-kanji","q":"ch 2  2 7 2 8  the bonfire  the apology  and the river vote evening at camp  yamauchi s matches have failed for the last time","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p85-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p85-1\">Ch.2 §2.7–2.8: the bonfire, the apology, and the river vote<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.85–92<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Evening at camp; Yamauchi&#x27;s matches have failed for the last time.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#shinohara-satsuki\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Takes over without being asked — dead leaves, thin twigs, then thicker branches — and the fire is up &quot;in the blink of an eye.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.85–86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> The bonfire doubles as a smoke signal: &quot;If you can see the smoke, you’ll be able to find the campsite even if you get lost.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.86<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> Walks the apology himself before she can: &quot;I was pushy because I wanted to save points. I’m sorry.&quot; — and remembers the first awful family camping toilet to explain why he now gets the girls&#x27; side.<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Shinohara Satsuki<\/b> She answers in kind; Ayanokōji reads the pair as having &quot;made up.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Runs the river-water vote as a free poll, not a whip; when Shinohara hesitates he offers Sudou&#x27;s boiling plan as the on-ramp; nearly half the boys raise hands, then the girls, then everyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.91–92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Takes the formal camp job — &quot;W-well, I guess if you ask, I gotta cooperate&quot; — the class&#x27;s only camping expertise on payroll.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Ogles Sakura&#x27;s body with Yamauchi blocking the view; the chapter keeps the leering and the competence in the same character without joining them.<span class=\"pg\">p.97<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p13-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.0 &amp; §2.4: the cruise loudmouth who turns out to be the useful one<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the chips at his feet<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner","w":"ike-kanji hirata-yousuke ibuki-mio kushida-kikyou ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 2  2 8  the points speech  the river vote  and kouenji s exit five o clock  kushida s group returns with fruit  the bonfire is up  and the class settles into its first night  on kouenji s retirement   maybe he didn t care about reaching class a  if it made his life easier  losing thirty points didn t matter at all","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1\">Ch.2 §2.8: the points speech, the river vote, and Kouenji&#x27;s exit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.87–98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Five o&#x27;clock; Kushida&#x27;s group returns with fruit, the bonfire is up, and the class settles into its first night.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q inner\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> On Kouenji&#x27;s retirement: &quot;Maybe he didn&#x27;t care about reaching Class A. If it made his life easier, losing thirty points didn&#x27;t matter at all.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Credits Ike, not himself, for the fire: &quot;You should be thanking Ike, not me.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.88<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Tries to raise the Ibuki report during the excitement and gets no opening: &quot;I didn&#x27;t have any chance to butt in.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.90<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Keeps his word to her while the class votes on river water.<span class=\"pg\">p.91<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Raises his hand for the river last, with Horikita, after everyone else — the chapter frames it as compliance, not conviction.<span class=\"pg\">p.92<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Backs the fishing-rod plan as the cheap test it is: &quot;the cost was so minimal that it couldn&#x27;t really hurt us.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.6–2.7: Ibuki, and the decision not to leave her<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\">→ After: Ch.3: the camera in the luggage, the morning watch, Kanzaki&#x27;s visit<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-satou-maya-y1v3-p93-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ibuki-mio satou-maya","q":"ch 2  2 8  she spots the interloper evening at the river camp  during the food discussion   by the way  that girl  ibuki san from class c  i ve seen her before    eyed ibuki with suspicion from across the camp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-satou-maya-y1v3-p93-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.2 §2.8: she spots the interloper<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.93<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#satou-maya\">Satō Maya<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Evening at the river camp, during the food discussion.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Satō Maya<\/b> “By the way… That girl, Ibuki-san from Class C? I’ve seen her before.” — eyed Ibuki with suspicion from across the camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Her naming is what moves Ibuki from background problem to class agenda; Yamauchi then supplies the explanation.<span class=\"pg\">p.93<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"chabashira-sae","q":"ch 2  2 8  she announces the retirement","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html#sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p97-1\">Ch.2 §2.8: she announces the retirement<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.97–98<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/chabashira-sae.html\">Chabashira Sae<\/a><\/span><\/h3><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> Reads the class the cost of Kouenji&#x27;s exit without inflection: &quot;Kouenji complained about being in poor physical condition and returned to the ship. Of course, that means that you’ve had thirty points deducted. Those are the rules, so there’s nothing to be done.&quot;<span class=\"pg\">p.97–98<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-chabashira-sae-y1v3-p24-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.1: she runs the rules that sink the summer<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio hirata-yousuke kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  the camera in the luggage  the morning watch  kanzaki s visit pre dawn heat in the class d tent  ayanokoji slips out while the class sleeps and goes through the piled luggage   i guess if i had to pick  school life s my priority  besides  i don t think it s possible to reach class a","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\">Ch.3: the camera in the luggage, the morning watch, Kanzaki&#x27;s visit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.100–104<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Pre-dawn heat in the Class D tent; Ayanokōji slips out while the class sleeps and goes through the piled luggage.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I guess if I had to pick, school life&#x27;s my priority. Besides, I don&#x27;t think it&#x27;s possible to reach Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The island morning: the mesh tent keeps the night breeze, the luggage is stacked outside to save space, and dawn comes on hot.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Opens Ibuki&#x27;s singularly colored bag and finds a digital camera with a rental sticker — “This item wasn&#x27;t appropriate for a deserted island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Checks the camera&#x27;s power source — “It had no data, and no sign that it&#x27;d been used.” — returns it to the bag, and reasons out why she would carry it.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The camera explains the dull sound he heard when she dropped the bag against a tree the day before.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Shares the early watch with Hirata while the rest of the class sleeps on.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After everyone is asleep, cuts one of the manual&#x27;s five blank pages, replicates a simple island map, folds it into a small square and pockets it.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Reads the heart-bedazzled gifts in Hirata&#x27;s pack as Karuizawa&#x27;s.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Meets Kanzaki at the river with Hirata and takes in the Class B campsite directions.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Weighs that Kanzaki, Ichinose and Horikita had worked together in the false accusation case — probably why he thinks they are still on good terms.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Reads the visit as reconnaissance — “You could estimate the number of points spent just by the number of toilets, showers, and tents.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The second spot update was postponed so ownership expires right after eight o&#x27;clock, letting the roll-call crowds camouflage the renewal.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.8: the points speech, the river vote, and Kouenji&#x27;s exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: Class C comes to provoke<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka karuizawa-kei kanzaki-ryuuji hirata-yousuke","q":"ch 3  the morning watch and the point arithmetic awake before the class in the crowded tent  greets ayanokoji slipping out  his back aching without a mattress   if you include kouenji kun s penalty  we spent almost 100 points yesterday  i told everyone that in the worst possible outcome we d be left with 120 points  but now i m not even sure about that  i guess the anxiety woke me   i m only doing this because i like it  if my hard work makes everyone in class happy  then i m satisfied  but it s surprisingly difficult   i wonder if our strategy s wrong  even if we can t beat the other classes  i thought it d be good for us to unify on this test  that s the real reason i don t want them to discover our leader   thank you  coming from you  that honestly makes me really happy","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html#sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p100-1\">Ch.3: the morning watch and the point arithmetic<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.100–105<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Awake before the class in the crowded tent; greets Ayanokōji slipping out, his back aching without a mattress.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/karuizawa-kei.html\">Karuizawa Kei<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “If you include Kouenji-kun&#x27;s penalty, we spent almost 100 points yesterday. I told everyone that in the worst possible outcome we&#x27;d be left with 120 points, but now I&#x27;m not even sure about that. I guess the anxiety woke me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I&#x27;m only doing this because I like it. If my hard work makes everyone in class happy, then I&#x27;m satisfied. But it&#x27;s surprisingly difficult.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> “I wonder if our strategy&#x27;s wrong. Even if we can&#x27;t beat the other classes, I thought it&#x27;d be good for us to unify on this test. That&#x27;s the real reason I don&#x27;t want them to discover our leader.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>6 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Cannot answer the Class A question — “That&#x27;s hard to answer. Aiming for the upper classes means forcing everyone… I&#x27;m sorry, I need to think on it.”<span class=\"pg\">p.101–102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Adjusts his position so Ayanokōji can read the manual comfortably — “small acts of consideration” noted from the other side.<span class=\"pg\">p.101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Karuizawa Kei<\/b> Carries her heart-bedazzled gifts in his pack and confirms it — “Spot on. How&#x27;d you guess?”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Greets Kanzaki by name and accepts the apology for the early visit.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Thank you. Coming from you, that honestly makes me really happy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Plans the sleeping-arrangement poll at the river, then after roll call assigns roles to the reliable students — Class D&#x27;s point-saving start.<span class=\"pg\">p.104–105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-hirata-yousuke-y1v3-p63-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.4–2.8: the river, the 120-point speech, and taking Ibuki in<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ibuki-mio","q":"ch 3  the camera in her bag the luggage pile outside the tent before dawn  her singularly colored bag is easy to spot","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\">Ch.3: the camera in her bag<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.100<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The luggage pile outside the tent before dawn; her singularly colored bag is easy to spot.<\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>1 more note<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Her rented digital camera — no data, no sign it was ever used — is found in the bag while she sleeps and put back untouched.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p78-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.6–§2.8: the Class C girl with the swollen cheek<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: the visit to the campsite<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p103-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"hirata-yousuke ayanokouji-kiyotaka kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"ch 3  the river meeting appears at the river with two class b boys in the early morning  surprised to meet class d up and out   first day s over  so i wondered how you were doing  i thought i d check on you  your location s great   did i surprise you  i m sorry  i m not here to cause trouble   there are large broken trees along the path from here to the beach  if you enter the forest to the southwest and walk a bit  you can find our campsite  you shouldn t get lost if you enter by those large trees  if you need something  go ahead and tell her you can come by","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p103-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p103-1\">Ch.3: the river meeting<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.103<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Appears at the river with two Class B boys in the early morning, surprised to meet Class D up and out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “First day&#x27;s over, so I wondered how you were doing. I thought I&#x27;d check on you. Your location&#x27;s great.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “Did I surprise you? I&#x27;m sorry, I&#x27;m not here to cause trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> “There are large broken trees along the path from here to the beach. If you enter the forest to the southwest and walk a bit, you can find our campsite. You shouldn&#x27;t get lost if you enter by those large trees. If you need…”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Apologizes to him directly; Hirata greets him by name.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Gives Ayanokōji the Class B campsite location without hesitating.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There are large broken trees along the path from here to the beach. If you enter the forest to the southwest and walk a bit, you can find our campsite. You shouldn&#x27;t get lost if you enter by those large trees. If you need something, go ahead and tell her you can come by.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The invitation names no one — the her is read across as Ichinose from the false-accusation case, an inference on Ayanokōji&#x27;s side.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p117-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: at his own camp while Class D visits<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"ike-kanji ibuki-mio horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 1  class c comes to provoke morning roll call over  exploration begins  two class c boys stride into the campsite eating chips","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: Class C comes to provoke<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Morning roll call over, exploration begins; two Class C boys stride into the campsite eating chips.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Recognizes Komiya and Kondou and recalls their earlier fight with Sudō as acting on Ryūen&#x27;s orders rather than just looking for a fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The campsite after roll call, the river base holding, Class D setting out to explore.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Stands with Ike when the chips are tossed at his feet; neither takes the bait until Hirata&#x27;s group returns.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Files Ibuki&#x27;s worst-case remark and decides telling Horikita “seemed like a good idea.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Pulls the leader out of the tent — “You&#x27;ve got eyes on Ryuuen, and you&#x27;ve even been observing Ichinose. People will remember that you&#x27;re the student council president&#x27;s younger sister. No matter what you do, you&#x27;ll be a target.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the camera in the luggage, the morning watch, Kanzaki&#x27;s visit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: Ryūen&#x27;s beach, spent to zero<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio","q":"ch 3  3 1  the visit to the campsite class c s boys stride into the campsite  a pained expression flashes across her face and she ducks behind the tent to hide   do you know ryuuen   i don t think they were looking for me   i wonder if things are heading toward that worst case scenario i imagined","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html#sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p105-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the visit to the campsite<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–106<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class C&#x27;s boys stride into the campsite; a pained expression flashes across her face and she ducks behind the tent to hide.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “Do you know Ryuuen?”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “I don&#x27;t think they were looking for me.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> “I wonder if things are heading toward that worst-case scenario I imagined…”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Sounds irritated discussing him — “as if she were discussing a family enemy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Komiya and Kondou are his underlings; his name alone puts her behind the tent.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ibuki-mio-y1v3-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the camera in her bag<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"komiya-kyogo ike-kanji","q":"ch 3  3 1  the chips at his feet the provocation reaches him in the middle of the campsite   what the hell  you guys","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html#sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p105-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: the chips at his feet<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–106<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The provocation reaches him in the middle of the campsite.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#komiya-kyogo\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> “What the hell, you guys?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> The chips bag lands at his feet; he snaps at the two Class C boys for ten minutes until Hirata&#x27;s group returns and they leave.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> The visit is aimed at his temper — Komiya and Kondou keep snacking while they bait him.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ike-kanji-y1v3-p85-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.7–2.8: the bonfire, the apology, and the river vote<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-komiya-kyogo-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ike-kanji kondou-reo komiya-kyogo","q":"ch 3  3 1  the campsite visit strides into the class d campsite with kondo  chips and soda in hand  smug grins on   wow  you class d rejects are really living frugal  eh  i guess that s what i d expect from a class of defectives   we have a message from ryuuen san  if you want to enjoy your summer vacation to the fullest  come to the beach right now  don t hang back  if you re sick of living like idiots  then we re happy to share our luxuries","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-komiya-kyogo-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1: the campsite visit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–106<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#komiya-kyogo\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Strides into the Class D campsite with Kondō, chips and soda in hand, smug grins on.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kondou-reo\">Kondō Reo<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> “Wow, you Class D rejects are really living frugal, eh? I guess that&#x27;s what I&#x27;d expect from a class of defectives.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> “We have a message from Ryuuen-san. If you want to enjoy your summer vacation to the fullest, come to the beach right now. Don&#x27;t hang back. If you&#x27;re sick of living like idiots, then we&#x27;re happy to share our luxuries.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation voices the taunt and the whole visit to the pair without saying which of them speaks.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Tosses a bag of potato chips near Ike&#x27;s feet and keeps snacking for ten minutes until Hirata&#x27;s group returns.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Bait him directly; he snaps and they ignore him.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kondō Reo<\/b> Enters with Kondō; their voices are never separated on these pages.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The pair who once fought Sudō, recalled as acting on Ryūen&#x27;s orders rather than looking for a fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kondou-reo-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"komiya-kyogo kondou-reo","q":"ch 3  3 1  the campsite visit follows komiya into the class d campsite during the morning provocation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kondou-reo-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.1: the campsite visit<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–106<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kondou-reo\">Kondō Reo<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Follows Komiya into the Class D campsite during the morning provocation.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#komiya-kyogo\">Komiya Kyogo<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Komiya Kyogo<\/b> Partner in every line of the visit — the taunts, the chip toss, the message — the translation never separates their voices.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> One of the two who fought Sudō; Ayanokōji recalls them as “acting on orders from Ryuuen, rather than just looking for a fight.”<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 1  called out of the tent summoned from the girls  tent after the class c provocation  the cloth moves  and she steps out   the cheap provocation coming from class c  yes  i heard   i don t want to move too much  since i m the leader  if i stand out too much  we ll be in a bad spot","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: called out of the tent<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.106–107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Summoned from the girls&#x27; tent after the Class C provocation; the cloth moves, and she steps out.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “The cheap provocation coming from Class C? Yes, I heard.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I don&#x27;t want to move too much. Since I&#x27;m the leader, if I stand out too much, we&#x27;ll be in a bad spot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Concedes she cannot stay hidden — the president&#x27;s younger sister, seen watching Ryūen and Ichinose: “You&#x27;re right. I suppose I can&#x27;t say what&#x27;s correct. Fine. I&#x27;m rather concerned about the state of the other classes. Let&#x27;s go.”<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> Takes his read that hiding will not change anything and sets out with him for the Class C beach.<span class=\"pg\">p.107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p73-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.5 &amp; §2.8: she refuses the assistantship, and votes last<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: the confrontation on the beach<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 2  ryuen s beach  spent to zero the class c beach  temporary toilets and showers  a tarp  a barbecue  chairs  a parasol  jet skis on the shoreline   it s up to you  horikita   that s simple  he d just do what kouenji did","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: Ryūen&#x27;s beach, spent to zero<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.108–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The Class C beach: temporary toilets and showers, a tarp, a barbecue, chairs, a parasol, jet skis on the shoreline.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It&#x27;s up to you, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “That&#x27;s simple. He&#x27;d just do what Kouenji did.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The Class C shore: cooking smoke, laughter, a hundred and fifty points or more already burned.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line names Horikita as the one addressed; the translation never tags the speaker.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands through Ryūen pouring out his water and throwing the warm bottle back at Ishizaki without intervening.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Leaves with her after the first-name call and the crotch-grab provocation, stopping once on the way back to look over the Class C camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Works out the zero-points strategy: nothing left to penalize, and even guesses of every rival leader&#x27;s identity could gain only “a maximum of 150 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The plan at zero points is retirement — “His physical condition was poor and he was mentally unstable. In that case, it&#x27;s better to just retire.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The walk-back exchange never tags its speakers until Horikita&#x27;s final line; these lines are recorded here as the responses to her questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: Class C comes to provoke<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.3: walking back from the Class C shore<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ibuki-mio horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 2  the confrontation on the beach the class c beach spectacle  she cannot believe what she is looking at   no way  all this stuff  is it even possible   if the person on top is incompetent  those below him will suffer  this is pitiful   we re trying to warn you  you re an idiot   there is one more piece of business  you know ibuki  of course   you used up all your points on the first day  didn t you   see you later  suzune   i don t know where exactly you found that out  but do not call me by my first name so casually","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: the confrontation on the beach<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.108–114<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The Class C beach spectacle; she cannot believe what she is looking at.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “No way… All this stuff… Is it even possible?”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “If the person on top is incompetent, those below him will suffer. This is pitiful,”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “We&#x27;re trying to warn you. You&#x27;re an idiot.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>8 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> Walks up to his chair with Ayanokōji and holds the confrontation to the end.<span class=\"pg\">p.109–114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The translation leaves the line untagged; his reply is thrown back at her.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Asks who hit Ibuki roundabout — “Her face is swollen. Who did that to her?” — and gets the admission of a light punishment.<span class=\"pg\">p.112–113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “There is one more piece of business. You know Ibuki, of course?”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You…used up all your points on the first day, didn&#x27;t you?”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “See you later, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I don&#x27;t know where exactly you found that out, but do not call me by my first name so casually.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Also untagged; she is the one addressed by the first-name call.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p106-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: called out of the tent<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: the walk back, and Class B’s camp<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p109-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio horikita-suzune ishizaki-daichi ryuuen-kakeru","q":"ch 3  3 2  the beach at zero holds court on the class c beach in swimwear   tanned  laid back in his chair  flashing white teeth   just as you see  we re enjoying our summer vacation   hmm  well  i didn t make a precise calculation   class d  the lowest of all  has to put up with starvation  heat  and futility just to save a measly 100 or 200 class points  it makes me laugh   i said to bring me cold water  this water s warm   cooperation  don t make me laugh  people betray each other with ease  people lie  relationships built on trust just aren t viable  you can only trust yourself   i absolutely loathe hard work  patience  saving  you must be joking   ah  she ran out of here rather suddenly  she went looking for help from another class in the end  pathetic girl   another boy defied me as well  so i had him driven out  i heard he didn t die  so he s probably off somewhere eating grass and insects to survive   ha ha ha  what should i do  i wonder  well  i suppose that plain  ordinary people can only engage in plain  ordinary thinking   see you later  suzune   well  i rather like forceful women  i ll make you submit to me eventually  when that time comes  it will be the ultimate pleasure","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p109-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html#sc-ryuuen-kakeru-y1v3-p109-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: the beach at zero<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.109–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Holds court on the Class C beach in swimwear — tanned, laid back in his chair, flashing white teeth.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#ishizaki-daichi\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Just as you see. We&#x27;re enjoying our summer vacation.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Hmm. Well, I didn&#x27;t make a precise calculation,”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Class D, the lowest of all, has to put up with starvation, heat, and futility just to save a measly 100 or 200 class points. It makes me laugh.”<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>14 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Pours his remaining water on the sand “almost in provocation” while Ishizaki fetches another bottle.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I said to bring me cold water. This water&#x27;s warm.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> “Ryuuen&#x27;s pupils were just like those of a snake.” — the returned bottle comes back in Ishizaki&#x27;s face.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Cooperation? Don&#x27;t make me laugh. People betray each other with ease. People lie. Relationships built on trust just aren&#x27;t viable. You can only trust yourself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I absolutely loathe hard work. Patience? Saving? You must be joking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. She ran out of here rather suddenly. She went looking for help from another class in the end? Pathetic girl.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Admits her light punishment was a slap — he gestures it — and offers forgiveness only on his terms: “If she grovels on the ground, I&#x27;ll forgive her. I&#x27;ve a tolerant heart.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Another boy defied me as well, so I had him driven out. I heard he didn&#x27;t die, so he&#x27;s probably off somewhere eating grass and insects to survive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Spent the entire three-hundred-point budget on day one — “Yes, as you said. I used all of our points.” — so there is nothing left to penalize.<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ha ha ha. What should I do, I wonder? Well, I suppose that plain, ordinary people can only engage in plain, ordinary thinking.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Calls her by her first name against her refusal, and answers her disgust while touching himself under the bathing suit.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “See you later, Suzune.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, I rather like forceful women. I&#x27;ll make you submit to me eventually. When that time comes, it will be the ultimate pleasure.”<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/b> Treats his fetch-boy as furniture — the warm bottle is thrown back at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y1v3-p111-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ryuuen-kakeru ishizaki-daichi","q":"ch 3  3 2  the warm water volleyball on the class c beach until ryuen calls him over to serve   i said to bring me cold water  this water s warm","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ishizaki-daichi-y1v3-p111-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.2: the warm water<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.111–112<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#ishizaki-daichi\">Ishizaki Daichi<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Volleyball on the Class C beach until Ryūen calls him over to serve.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “I said to bring me cold water. This water&#x27;s warm.”<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>2 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Rushes sweat-dripping to the tent and hands over a bottle; Ryūen pours it out and throws it back at him.<span class=\"pg\">p.111<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> “Ishizaki&#x27;s body stiffened.” at the snake-pupil hum; he picks the bottle up and runs back to the tent.<span class=\"pg\">p.112<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"inner spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  walking back from the class c shore on the path inland past the beach  he turns to scan the class c shore once more while the walk back is still arguing over what ryuen s spending means   the test is literally about freedom  ryuuen s way of thinking is one way to approach it  it seems like ibuki and another student rebelled  and because of that class c will lose twenty points a day  since he knew he d be losing that many points every day no matter what  he came up with a drastic strategy   since i didn t know when ryuuen had decided to spend all of class c s points  i could only guess   we ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up  ryuuen is most definitely wrong  i cannot possibly understand him   a zero point strategy  huh  i see  that s really interesting","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\">Ch.3: walking back from the Class C shore<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.116<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">On the path inland past the beach, he turns to scan the Class C shore once more while the walk back is still arguing over what Ryūen&#x27;s spending means.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “The test is literally about freedom. Ryuuen’s way of thinking is one way to approach it. It seems like Ibuki and another student rebelled, and because of that Class C will lose twenty points a day. Since he knew he’d be losing…”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “We ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up. Ryuuen is most definitely wrong. I cannot possibly understand him,”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “A zero-point strategy, huh? I see. That’s really interesting.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “The test is literally about freedom. Ryuuen’s way of thinking is one way to approach it. It seems like Ibuki and another student rebelled, and because of that Class C will lose twenty points a day. Since he knew he’d be losing that many points every day no matter what, he came up with a drastic strategy.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> “Since I didn’t know when Ryuuen had decided to spend all of Class C’s points, I could only guess.”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The walk-back exchange is never tagged; her line is confirmed by the narration that follows it, and both of his stand as the remarks she answers.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Reads winning as more than saving the class&#x27;s own points: dissent inside the group would have to be silenced before a zero-points route could work.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: Ryūen&#x27;s beach, spent to zero<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.3: Class B’s camp at the well<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ichinose-honami hirata-yousuke horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 3  the walk back  and class b s camp walking inland from the class c shore  she is still arguing over ryuen s spending when the visit to class b s camp begins   we ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up  ryuuen is most definitely wrong  i cannot possibly understand him   i was wondering if it might behoove us to tentatively enter into a cooperative relationship  like last time   yeah  there s a lot to make us uneasy right now  but we have to try and make it through   i was thinking that we should talk about that  too  if we didn t have to be on guard with even one class  we d really appreciate it  as long as you don t mind  ichinose san  i d like you to accept the proposal   this class has fallen in line far better than i could have imagined  i suppose that s because you re the one taking command  right   no  we do have a boy named hirata  though  everyone in class clusters around him   ichinose san  i m terribly sorry to keep asking you questions  but we want to confirm class a s status  can you tell us anything that will help us capture their base camp  even something you know about the area might really help   secretive  what kind of measures has class a taken   you can t use any sly tricks in this test  ryuuen has most definitely spent almost all of their points  they might be having fun right now  but they re going to regret it later   i think it s about time to get going  ayanokouji kun  we ll be a bother to class b if we linger too long   ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: the walk back, and Class B’s camp<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.116–125<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Walking inland from the Class C shore, she is still arguing over Ryūen&#x27;s spending when the visit to Class B&#x27;s camp begins.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “We ought to think of a way to get points back without giving up. Ryuuen is most definitely wrong. I cannot possibly understand him,”<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I was wondering if it might behoove us to tentatively enter into a cooperative relationship, like last time,”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “Yeah. There’s a lot to make us uneasy right now, but we have to try and make it through.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>18 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Rejects the zero-points route on principle: points are to be won back, not written off.<span class=\"pg\">p.116<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Arrives as a visitor with Ayanokōji and declines the hammock offer, so Ichinose sits instead.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Listens through the whole tour — well, water shower, toilet, vinyl, heat — without interrupting.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Afterward lays out Class D&#x27;s situation completely, holding nothing back in the interest of fairness.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I was thinking that we should talk about that, too. If we didn’t have to be on guard with even one class, we’d really appreciate it. As long as you don’t mind, Ichinose-san, I’d like you to accept the proposal.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The cooperation exchange is untagged; she is the one addressing Ichinose by name, and Ichinose&#x27;s proposal and reply are recorded under her.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “This class has fallen in line far better than I could have imagined. I suppose that’s because you’re the one taking command, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Judges Class B by its order: every student carrying out a role, and doing the duty happily, with nobody trying to skip out.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. We do have a boy named Hirata, though. Everyone in class clusters around him.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Names him as the one Class D gathers around, then changes the topic.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ichinose-san. I’m terribly sorry to keep asking you questions, but we want to confirm Class A’s status. Can you tell us anything that will help us capture their base camp? Even something you know about the area might really help.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Secretive? What kind of measures has Class A taken?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You can’t use any sly tricks in this test. Ryuuen has most definitely spent almost all of their points. They might be having fun right now, but they’re going to regret it later.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line is untagged; the narration that follows anchors the withheld withdrawal plan on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think it’s about time to get going, Ayanokouji-kun. We’ll be a bother to Class B if we linger too long.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “In general, I think we’re all on the same page, but they’re further ahead. I can’t deny it,”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Says it as a declaration of defeat: the distance between D and B is not only a matter of points.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The two untagged verdict lines that follow are left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p108-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.2: the confrontation on the beach<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: talking past Class A at the cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune kaneda-satoru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 3  class b s camp at the well deep forest past the broken landmark tree  class b s base is set around a well with hammocks strung between the trees  ichinose tying a cord  kanzaki sitting a little way off   well  i suppose it s just what we d expect from class b   your class seems to be functioning well  despite obstacles   i m sorry if we re getting in the way   what s a water shower  i m a little curious about that   did you already know about them  water showers  i mean   a class c student   i think it s about time to get going  ayanokouji kun  we ll be a bother to class b if we linger too long","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: Class B’s camp at the well<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.117–125<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deep forest past the broken landmark tree: Class B&#x27;s base is set around a well with hammocks strung between the trees, Ichinose tying a cord, Kanzaki sitting a little way off.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kaneda-satoru\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well, I suppose it’s just what we’d expect from Class B…”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Your class seems to be functioning well, despite obstacles.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m sorry if we’re getting in the way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> Class B&#x27;s site — trees around a well, hammocks instead of tents, and a path of student tracks already beaten through the forest.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the broken tree as a landmark the school left on purpose, which is why Kanzaki&#x27;s directions needed no detail.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The three lines are untagged; Ichinose takes up and answers each of them.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She reads the visit as a request and welcomes them without any hint of protest.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s a water shower? I’m a little curious about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Judges the water shower probably less effective than the temporary shower because it costs five points less, and passes on it.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you already know about them? Water showers, I mean,”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> Class B&#x27;s purchases itemize to exactly seventy points once the food is counted.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Sets that total against Class D with Kōenji&#x27;s retirement already deducted.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Weighs the foraging against the fruit Kushida&#x27;s group carried back for Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Watches the Class B method in one pass: the well tested before anyone drinks, hot water on a gas can, unlimited vinyl sheets granted with the temporary toilet, and water sprinkled to pull the heat out of the soil.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He stays silent while she lays out Class D&#x27;s side and runs the exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The visitors&#x27; questions about hard ground and the heat are never tagged and are left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Names him as a Class C student before Ichinose can finish answering.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A Class C student?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Files him as the Class C boy who resisted Ryūen and was taken in by Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think it’s about time to get going, Ayanokouji-kun. We’ll be a bother to Class B if we linger too long.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Says farewell with Horikita and leaves the camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Sets Class D against Class B on the way out: Class D has selfish students like Kōenji who run off alone, and nobody with the power to step in.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The two untagged verdict lines that follow the departure are left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.3: walking back from the Class C shore<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the Class A cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p117-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke kaneda-satoru ichinose-honami","q":"ch 3  3 3  the camp that already works class b s base around the well  she is tying a hammock cord to a tree when horikita and ayanokoji walk in  and kanzaki sits a little way off   huh  horikita san  and ayanokouji kun   ha ha  yeah  it was really difficult at first  but we tried a bunch of different things  and it worked out  though the list of chores just keeps on increasing  there s still a ton of work left   oh  i m sorry  that probably sounded like i was trying to drive you guys away  i think it s all right if you hang around for a while  you probably came here to ask me something  right   i think so  too   hammocks  cookware  small tent  lantern  and temporary toilet  fishing rod  a water shower  if we combine those items with the food we purchased  the total comes to exactly seventy points   well  let s go over the situation bit by bit  shall we  since there are various places in the woods where we can find fruits and vegetables  we can compensate for deficiencies in points by foraging for food  we can also head out to the sea and fish  that s what i was thinking we d do for food  we re not worried about water  since we have a well   at first we were worried whether the water was safe to drink    starting this morning  we had everyone use the   well to get water   also  there s enough natural water that we can use it for showers  that s what a water shower is   after we put water in the tank here  we get hot water in only a few seconds  it s really convenient  we use ","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p117-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: the camp that already works<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.117–125<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class B&#x27;s base around the well: she is tying a hammock cord to a tree when Horikita and Ayanokōji walk in, and Kanzaki sits a little way off.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kaneda-satoru\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Huh? Horikita-san? And Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Ha ha, yeah. It was really difficult at first! But we tried a bunch of different things, and it worked out. Though the list of chores just keeps on increasing. There’s still a ton of work left,”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Oh, I’m sorry. That probably sounded like I was trying to drive you guys away. I think it’s all right if you hang around for a while. You probably came here to ask me something, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>41 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> Class B&#x27;s site — trees around a well, hammocks strung for lack of tent space, unfamiliar equipment beside the water.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes the interruption as a welcome rather than an intrusion: smiling, she assumes they came with a question.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Welcomes them without any hint of protest and invites them to sit on the hammock.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think so, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The agreement is untagged; it answers Horikita&#x27;s proposal directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hammocks. Cookware. Small tent, lantern, and temporary toilet. Fishing rod, a water shower… If we combine those items with the food we purchased, the total comes to exactly seventy points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> Reads her class&#x27;s purchases aloud from a manual: seventy points in all.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, let’s go over the situation bit by bit, shall we? Since there are various places in the woods where we can find fruits and vegetables, we can compensate for deficiencies in points by foraging for food. We can also head out to the sea and fish. That’s what I was thinking we’d do for food. We’re not worried about water, since we have a well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Food comes from foraging and the sea; water comes from the well.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At first we were worried whether the water was safe to drink, … Starting this morning, we had everyone use the … well to get water.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Drinks from the well herself the day before, waits to see if she gets an upset stomach, and only then lets the class use it.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, there’s enough natural water that we can use it for showers. That’s what a water shower is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After we put water in the tank here, we get hot water in only a few seconds. It’s really convenient. We use a gas can for the heat source. When we run out, I plan to request another.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. This is the first I’ve heard about or used them. The school’s rules are rather scary, aren’t they? There weren’t any details in the manual, and we can’t ask the teacher, either. Thankfully we have some kids who are familiar with the outdoors in our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We set up this temporary toilet instead of getting a shower room. We got it so that the people who dislike being seen by others when they shower could have privacy. The fabric is also waterproof.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, yeah. At first, I wondered what we were going to do, but then we took appropriate measures. Want a look?”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Lifts the tent flap after warning the girls inside and shows the vinyl sheets underfoot — about two centimeters thick.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When we paid for the temporary toilet, we were told we had access to an unlimited number of vinyl sheets. So I might have asked for too many, but … we received a large number of them. Of course, I don’t want to waste resources, so I plan to put any unused vinyl sheets into one sheet, and return them in the end.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder if it’s because we sprinkle water around. We’ve sprinkled water near our beds, because they’re close to the well. We put some water in the plastic bottles that people drank from, and then everyone carries them around so they can sprinkle water efficiently. The water soaks into the soil quite easily, and since it takes some time for it to evaporate, the effect lingers and removes the heat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Beats the heat with sprinkled water rather than equipment — knowledge, not tools, is what makes the campsite work.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see… Having someone retire sounds like it really hurt you guys.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, can we continue our cooperative relationship? I thought it would be a good idea to ignore the rule about trying to find out the leader’s identity. What do you think?”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The cooperation exchange is untagged; the addressee anchors put these lines on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I’m okay with that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Reaffirms the cooperative relationship with her and agrees to drop the hunt for the leader&#x27;s identity.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. For the time being, anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes the command credit only conditionally — for the time being.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Knows him from the soccer club and calls him really popular among the girls.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. From the soccer club! I know him, I know him! He’s really popular among the girls.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, if you’re okay with something that might be useful, I can tell you something about their place. However, obtaining information is going to be tough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just after you cut through this area, there’s an opening. Turn right and go straight until you see a cave. That’s probably where the Class A base camp is. I went there myself to investigate, but I don’t know for sure. It’s because they’re so thoroughly defensive…or rather, secretive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Has already scouted the Class A site herself and marks it as thoroughly defensive.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Honestly, seeing is believing. If you take a look yourselves, you’ll understand right away. Since you two are going to check on Class A, does that mean you already understand Class C’s situation?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her assessment of Class C — no intention of taking the test seriously, five days left, no spot even looked for — runs untagged between her question and the narration that follows; it is left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Takes his interruption patiently, tells him where Nakanishi is, and sends him after Chihiro-chan&#x27;s group.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think Nakanishi-kun headed down to the shore. Why do you ask?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh no, not at all. I’m really happy you feel that way, Kaneda-kun. Can you head over and follow Chihiro-chan’s group? If you tell them I told you to do so, it’ll be okay.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you know him? It looks like he had some kind of dispute with Class C. He said he’d get by on his own, but I couldn’t just leave him. I haven’t asked him about his situation yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes in a Class C boy nobody else would take because she couldn&#x27;t just leave him — and has not yet asked him what happened.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hardens when she hears that Ibuki was hit — the narration calls it strengthening her resolve to protect her class.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Closes the visit with farewells after the full exchange of information.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p117-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"","w":"ichinose-honami kanzaki-ryuuji","q":"ch 3  3 3  at his own camp while class d visits sitting a little way off from ichinose when class d walks into the class b camp","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html#sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p117-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: at his own camp while Class D visits<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.117, p.120<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Sitting a little way off from Ichinose when Class D walks into the Class B camp.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/p><details class=\"more\"><summary>3 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He says nothing during the visit; the pages place him in the background of the scene.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Ayanokōji credits him with having deduced Class D&#x27;s spending from what he saw at the river that morning.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> The camp Class D found from his directions is hers; he stays out of the exchange while she runs it.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–120<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-kanzaki-ryuuji-y1v3-p103-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the river meeting<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-kaneda-satoru-y1v3-p124-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami ryuuen-kakeru kaneda-satoru","q":"ch 3  3 3  the class c boy who offers to help at class b s camp he interrupts ichinose in a reserved voice while horikita and ayanokoji are still there   pardon me  ichinose san  i m sorry to interrupt  do you know where nakanishi kun is   i thought i d offer to help  is that unnecessary   okay  thank you very much","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-kaneda-satoru-y1v3-p124-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.3: the Class C boy who offers to help<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.124<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#kaneda-satoru\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At Class B&#x27;s camp he interrupts Ichinose in a reserved voice while Horikita and Ayanokōji are still there.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/ryuuen-kakeru.html\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> “Pardon me, Ichinose-san? I’m sorry to interrupt. Do you know where Nakanishi-kun is?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> “I thought I’d offer to help. Is that unnecessary?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> “Okay. Thank you very much!”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> A Class C student estranged from his class for resisting Ryūen and sheltered by Class B; Horikita notices that he speaks to Ichinose with unusual formality.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Asks her for work, and she sends him to follow Chihiro-chan&#x27;s group.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ryūen Kakeru<\/b> The dispute with Ryūen that got him out of Class C; the pages say he claimed he would get by on his own.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> He has not told anyone his situation yet, and Ichinose says she has not asked him.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ch 3  3 4  the class a cave the cave mouth cut deep into the mountainside like a demon s mouth  with two temporary toilets and a shower room outside  he steps over horikita and walks up to it   let s go  i mean  it s class a  so of course we re going to be scared  there s nothing we can do about that   and what do we gain by trying to peek from our hiding spot  we can barely see  and there s no one around  there s not much we can see unless we enter the cave   i haven t thought of anything  come on  don t worry","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: the Class A cave<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.126–129<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The cave mouth cut deep into the mountainside like a demon&#x27;s mouth, with two temporary toilets and a shower room outside; he steps over Horikita and walks up to it.<\/p><p class=\"tags\"><a href=\"../../../world/uninhabited-island.html\">Uninhabited Island<\/a><\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Let’s go. I mean, it’s Class A, so of course we’re going to be scared. There’s nothing we can do about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “And what do we gain by trying to peek from our hiding spot? We can barely see, and there’s no one around. There’s not much we can see unless we enter the cave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I haven’t thought of anything. Come on, don’t worry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The Class A site: a cave in the mountainside, its entrance hidden behind vinyl sheets joined into one giant tarp.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Goes up openly rather than scouting from cover so that he can see inside — and finds the tarp already blocking the view.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The opening line on the approach is untagged; Horikita&#x27;s two questions are recorded under her.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Recognizes Yahiko as one of the two who found the cave on the first day; Katsuragi is away.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The closing judgment — that Class A has to be left alone and cannot be investigated — is his, left untagged and recorded here without a quotation.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: Class B’s camp at the well<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko katsuragi-kouhei horikita-suzune","q":"ch 3  3 4  talking past class a at the cave she and ayanokoji walk up to the class a cave together after watching from a distance fails to show anything   what are you planning  we gain nothing by carelessly exposing ourselves   we came to snoop  you have a problem   i mean  i would ve thought that since you re in class a you d be clever  but   well  rather than clever  i d say you re underhanded  what cowardly methods   i m horikita  from class d   stupid  huh  in that case  there s no harm in us seeing what s inside  right  or does that make you feel uncomfortable   so it s not a problem if we look  you re in the way   we re just going to look inside  that itself isn t a violation of the rules  right   oh  so you occupy this place  i didn t know that  is there a device inside   well  there definitely aren t any rules that say we can t go into the cave  it s certainly true that we cannot use the cave while it s being occupied  but that s not the same as the right to monopolize it or anything  we should have the right to look inside  or at least to verify if there s equipment  right  if we couldn t do that  then people could just forcibly monopolize every spot  that s not what this test is about   you re forcefully monopolizing control of the spot  the rules don t protect such actions   well  fine  i look forward to seeing the results  and class a s abilities","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html#sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p126-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: talking past Class A at the cave<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.126–129<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">She and Ayanokōji walk up to the Class A cave together after watching from a distance fails to show anything.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#katsuragi-kouhei\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “What are you planning? We gain nothing by carelessly exposing ourselves.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “We came to snoop. You have a problem?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> “I mean, I would’ve thought that since you’re in Class A you’d be clever, but…”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>17 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The approach dialogue is untagged; the question-and-answer chain, and the question tagged to her at the end of it, put these on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Switches into a deliberate provocation — the narration calls it a daring switch flipped in her brain.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, rather than clever, I’d say you’re underhanded. What cowardly methods.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’m Horikita, from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stupid, huh? In that case, there’s no harm in us seeing what’s inside, right? Or does that make you feel uncomfortable?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So it’s not a problem if we look? You’re in the way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We’re just going to look inside. That itself isn’t a violation of the rules, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh? So you occupy this place. I didn’t know that. Is there a device inside?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Provokes him on purpose and talks past every block he puts up.<span class=\"pg\">p.127–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, there definitely aren’t any rules that say we can’t go into the cave. It’s certainly true that we cannot use the cave while it’s being occupied, but that’s not the same as the right to monopolize it or anything. We should have the right to look inside, or at least to verify if there’s equipment, right? If we couldn’t do that, then people could just forcibly monopolize every spot. That’s not what this test is about.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> The monopoly argument: occupation bars use, not looking, and a spot that nobody may inspect could be seized by anyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re forcefully monopolizing control of the spot. The rules don’t protect such actions.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Both p.128 lines are untagged; the second is answered by Katsuragi conceding the point.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Matched and stopped by his unspoken-rule argument.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, fine. I look forward to seeing the results, and Class A’s abilities.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Leaves with the wind knocked out of her; without Katsuragi&#x27;s arrival she would have gone through the vinyl.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her mutters “W-wait.” and “Ugh, what an unintelligible, half-assed answer.” are untagged; the second answers his own admission.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-horikita-suzune-y1v3-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: the walk back, and Class B’s camp<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p126-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei totsuka-yahiko","q":"ch 3  3 4  holding the entrance at the class a cave entrance as class d approaches  the two temporary toilets and the shower room stand outside   who are you guys  what class are you from   what   hah  it s obvious you re from class d  you re a bunch of stupid failures  after all   that s not it at all   w wait  hey  wait  i said  don t just do whatever you please   stop screwing around  class a occupies this spot  class d doesn t have permission to use it   y yeah  so back off   huh   katsuragi san  these two came to snoop around our camp  they re a bunch of filthy losers   s sorry","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html#sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p126-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: holding the entrance<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.126–129<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">At the Class A cave entrance as Class D approaches; the two temporary toilets and the shower room stand outside.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#katsuragi-kouhei\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “Who are you guys? What class are you from?”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “What?”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> “Hah, it’s obvious you’re from Class D. You’re a bunch of stupid failures, after all.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>12 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Identified as the one of the pair who found the cave quickly on the first day.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not it at all!”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “W-wait! Hey! Wait, I said! Don’t just do whatever you please!”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Moves in front of Horikita to block her path.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Stop screwing around. Class A occupies this spot. Class D doesn’t have permission to use it!”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Y-yeah. So back off.”<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Huh?!”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Katsuragi-san! These two came to snoop around our camp! They’re a bunch of filthy losers!”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Irritated by her provocation and unable to stop her; she talks past every objection he makes.<span class=\"pg\">p.127–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “S-sorry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> Takes the rebuke — his answer to the provocation was exactly the bait it was meant to be.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Limit<\/span> Left holding the entrance alone when Katsuragi is away; the sharp one of the pair is absent until the end of the exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-totsuka-yahiko-y1v3-p59-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the second man in the cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p127-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko horikita-suzune katsuragi-kouhei","q":"ch 3  3 4  the parley at the cave named first as absent from the class a cave  then arriving at the entrance midway through the standoff with horikita   what are you doing  i don t recall giving you permission to invite guests   well then  it should be fine for you to look inside  however  prepare yourself  the moment you touch anything  i will notify the school and report your actions as obstruction toward another class  i can t guarantee what will happen to class d as a result   you re right about that  i cannot argue the point  however  it s something of an unspoken rule  you in class d have a spot by the river  class b has a well  you live in and surround the occupied space  so it s halfway monopolized  have you taken any forceful measures in dealing with trespassers to your area   one class occupies one spot  then  they continue to protect that spot so they may obtain points until the end of the test  if you violate this unspoken rule  it creates chaos  naturally  class a will trespass upon class d s base in retaliation  we should avoid trouble   we are quite capable  we also expect things from you  class d  by which i mean  your futile struggling","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p127-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\">Ch.3 §3.4: the parley at the cave<\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.127–129<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../../../people/index.html#katsuragi-kouhei\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Named first as absent from the Class A cave, then arriving at the entrance midway through the standoff with Horikita.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../../../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a> · <a href=\"../../../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “What are you doing? I don’t recall giving you permission to invite guests.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “Well then, it should be fine for you to look inside. However, prepare yourself. The moment you touch anything, I will notify the school and report your actions as obstruction toward another class. I can’t guarantee what will…”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Katsuragi Kōhei<\/b> “You’re right about that. I cannot argue the point. However, it’s something of an unspoken rule. You in Class D have a spot by the river. Class B has a well. You live in and surround the occupied space, so it’s halfway…”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The page introduces him as the sharp-witted one of the pair who found the cave on the first day.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, it should be fine for you to look inside. However, prepare yourself. The moment you touch anything, I will notify the school and report your actions as obstruction toward another class. I can’t guarantee what will happen to Class D as a result.”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Threatens a school report over touched vinyl — read as probably bluffing, with some genuine danger behind it.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re right about that. I cannot argue the point. However, it’s something of an unspoken rule. You in Class D have a spot by the river. Class B has a well. You live in and surround the occupied space, so it’s halfway monopolized. Have you taken any forceful measures in dealing with trespassers to your area?”<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Concedes the formal point and answers it with practice: every class already defends its own area.<span class=\"pg\">p.128<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “One class occupies one spot. Then, they continue to protect that spot so they may obtain points until the end of the test. If you violate this unspoken rule, it creates chaos. Naturally, Class A will trespass upon Class D’s base in retaliation. We should avoid trouble.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> States the island&#x27;s working rule: one spot per class, held for the whole test, or retaliation follows.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We are quite capable. We also expect things from you, Class D. By which I mean, your futile struggling.”<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Pulls his partner off the provocation: answer bait like that and the other side backs down.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Ends her advance with words; the narration has her stopped in her tracks by his calm.<span class=\"pg\">p.128–129<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> With him on the entrance, Class D&#x27;s only option is retreat — he has stripped every other one away.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-katsuragi-kouhei-y1v3-p59-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.3: the Class A leader who showed his card<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
